Scope
=====

The MIT license below covers the source code in this repository: every Python
script under `code/`, and the root-level `test_assertions.py`, `reproduce.sh`,
and `requirements.txt`.

It does not cover the following, and nothing in it should be read as granting
rights over them.

`code/aihub_subtropical/`: the result tables (`.csv` and `.json`)
    They derive from the AI Hub dataset, 국내 재배 아열대·열대 병해충 데이터
    (Domestically Cultivated Subtropical and Tropical Pest and Disease Data),
    which AI Hub distributes only to applicants it approves. The AI Hub usage
    policy (https://www.aihub.or.kr/intrcn/guid/usagepolicy.do) states that the
    AI data on AI Hub were built under the Intelligent Information Industry
    Infrastructure Development project of the Korean Ministry of Science and ICT
    and the National Information Society Agency (NIA). Their use is governed by
    that policy, not by this license. The policy requires every use of the data,
    and every derivative work, to state that the data are a result of NIA's
    project. It also requires a separate agreement with the institutions that
    built the data and NIA before an organization or individual located outside
    Korea uses the data, and before the data leave the country. The tables are
    published here so that the results reported in the accompanying paper can
    be checked.

`code/dacon_cropdisease/`: the result tables (`.csv`), `dacon_series_ids.parquet`,
and `dacon_granularity.json`
    They derive from the Crop Disease Diagnosis (CDD) dataset, which LG AI
    Research released through DACON's competition 235870
    (https://dacon.io/competitions/official/235870/overview/rules). Two of the
    tables also derive from the split files in the CDD study's repository
    (https://github.com/hyunseoki/crop_disease), which declares no license.
    Their use is governed by the competition's rules, not by this license. Those
    rules allow access to and use of the competition data only for
    non-commercial purposes, including academic research and education. They
    also bind participants not to transmit, copy, publish, redistribute, or
    provide the competition data to anyone who has not entered the competition.

`code/survey/survey_records.csv`
    The authors' coding of the fusion studies that the paper cites.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Sungwoo Kang. All rights reserved. The data availability
    statements that it quotes belong to the studies that published them.

The rest of `paper/`, and the Markdown documents in this repository
    The manuscript, its figures and parameter files, its bibliography, the
    README files, and `SOURCES.md`.
    Copyright (c) 2026 Sungwoo Kang. All rights reserved.


